# Networked Frontend Authoring Integration

This repository is `frontend-app-authoring`, the Open edX course-authoring MFE used by Networked. Treat it as the Studio-facing authoring UI only. Do not use this rule as the source of truth for `fe-main`, `be-main`, LMS learner APIs, user provisioning, enrollment, course discovery, or backend Open edX cookie storage except where this app directly depends on those contracts.

Networked users normally enter this MFE after `fe-main` sends them through the LMS login bridge:

`/auth/networked-login/<course_id>?token=<tokenId>&communityId=<communityId>&nextPage=add-lesson`

Open edX validates the Networked token, creates LMS/Studio browser sessions, then redirects to this app/Studio authoring page. This MFE should assume authentication and course access are already established by Open edX/Studio and Networked backend.

## App Role

`frontend-app-authoring` owns the browser UX for course creation after the course already exists in Open edX Studio:

- Course outline authoring at `/course/:courseId`.
- Section, lesson, unit, and component authoring.
- Lesson settings used by Networked, including unskippable units, minimum time on unit, answer visibility, and graded inclusion.
- Studio grading settings at `/course/:courseId/settings/grading`.
- Student overview and score board entry points when Studio routes/MFE config send users here.
- Networked-friendly header/navigation simplification.
- Calls from the browser to Studio/LMS/Networked backend only when this app has an explicit UI need.

Networked terminology maps to Open edX content like this:

- Networked "section" means Open edX `chapter`.
- Networked "lesson" means Open edX `sequential` subsection.
- Networked "unit" means Open edX `vertical`.
- Lesson content is made of XBlock components such as HTML/text, problem/question, video, SCORM, and other enabled block types.

## Networked Changes In This Repo

This fork is not a generic upstream `frontend-app-authoring` checkout. It has Networked-specific changes and expectations:

- The authoring experience is reduced to Networked-needed tabs/pages: course outline, student overview, score board, grading, and profile/community context.
- The Networked frontend should not expose "subsection" wording. In UI and rules, say `Section` for Open edX `chapter` and `Lesson` for Open edX `sequential`.
- Lesson settings are redesigned around a small Networked popup instead of the full upstream subsection settings tab set.
- `src/generic/configure-modal/ConfigureModal.jsx` renders a simplified `QuizSettings` body for `sequential` lessons and comments out the upstream Basic, Visibility, and Advanced tabs for that case.
- `src/generic/configure-modal/QuizSettings.jsx` owns Networked toggles for "Make this Unit Un-skippable", "Minimum time on Unit", "Show Answers on Result Page", and "Include in Graded".
- `src/course-outline/data/api.js` persists those lesson settings to Studio using `unskippable_unit`, `minimum_time_on_unit`, `show_correctness`, and `graderType`/`format`.
- `src/data/api.js` adds Networked backend calls for edit access and visibility/publish behavior through `HttpWrapper`.
- `src/helper/httpWrapper.ts` is a Networked-only API bridge from this MFE back to `be-main`; it forwards `openedxSessionToken` and `openedxCommunityId` cookies.
- `src/helper/constants.ts` chooses the Networked app/backend host from the current hostname: `lab`, `qa`/`local`, or production.

When maintaining this fork, treat those as intentional product decisions unless the task explicitly asks to restore upstream Studio behavior.

